---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const faqSchema = {
 "@context": "https://schema.org",
 "@type": "FAQPage",
 "mainEntity": [
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "How long does warm-up take?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Typically 4-6 weeks to reach substantial volume; transactional-only servers with strong engagement can move faster, cold outreach slower."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Do I need to warm up a subdomain?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "If it is newly created and will send at scale: yes. Reputation attaches to the sending identity, including subdomains."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Can warm-up tools help?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Engagement-based warm-up (automatic replies to simulated mail) has limited, debated value. Real engagement from real recipients is the durable path."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "What volume is 'safe' immediately?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Small: tens to low hundreds per day from a new identity. Volume is earned, not configured."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "Does DMARC need to be at reject before warm-up?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "No: p=none with reporting is correct during warm-up; enforcement comes after the identity stabilizes."
   }
  },
  {
   "@type": "Question",
   "name": "My warm-up was fine but mail went to spam in week 3. Why?",
   "acceptedAnswer": {
    "@type": "Answer",
    "text": "Volume outgrew engagement, or a content/link change tripped filters. Cut volume in half, raise engagement, then resume."
   }
  }
 ]
}
---
<BaseLayout
  title="How to Warm Up an Email Server or New Domain | PromptDNS"
  description="Email warm-up schedule: how to ramp a new server or domain from zero to full volume over 4-6 weeks without landing in spam."
  schema={[faqSchema]}
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-12">
    <nav class="mb-4 text-sm text-ink-faint" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-accent">Home</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <a href="/email-authentication/" class="hover:text-accent">Email Authentication</a>
       <span aria-hidden="true">/</span>
      <span class="text-ink-dim">Warm Up Email Server</span>
    </nav>
    <h1 class="font-display text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink sm:text-4xl">How to Warm Up an Email Server or New Domain</h1>
    <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Mailbox providers judge senders by history. A brand-new domain or IP has none, so the only safe strategy is to earn it: start small, deliver engagement, and ramp volume on a schedule. Rushing this is the single most common self-inflicted deliverability wound.</p>
    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">The 4-week ramp template</h2>
      <div class="overflow-x-auto rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60"><table class="pdns-table"><thead><tr><th>Week</th><th>Daily volume</th><th>Focus</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">1</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">10-50 to your most engaged contacts</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Openers who will reply: engagement signals build the base</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">2</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Double weekly</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Keep bounce rate under 2%; watch spam-folder placement</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">3</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Double again</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Introduce regular campaign content</td></tr><tr><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">4-6</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Reach target volume</td><td class="text-sm text-ink-dim">Only if placement and engagement stayed healthy</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Non-negotiables during warm-up</h2>
      <ul class="list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-5"><li>Authentication complete before message one: <a href="/spf-record/">SPF</a>, <a href="/dkim/">DKIM</a>, <a href="/dmarc/">DMARC</a> at p=none minimum.</li><li>Reverse DNS set on the sending IP, matching your HELO name.</li><li>Send to your <em>best</em> addresses first: recent openers and clickers, never scraped or purchased lists.</li><li>Keep complaint rates near zero; pause and investigate at the first spike.</li><li>Monitor placement: seed accounts or the Gmail "Why this message" view across providers.</li></ul>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Signs you are ramping too fast</h2>
      <p>Open rates collapsing mid-week, mail arriving in spam at Gmail/Outlook, or bounce codes shifting to policy rejections (5.7.x). The response is always the same: cut volume back to the last healthy level, hold for several days, then resume the ramp.</p>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <div class="mt-3 grid gap-3"><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">How long does warm-up take?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Typically 4-6 weeks to reach substantial volume; transactional-only servers with strong engagement can move faster, cold outreach slower.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Do I need to warm up a subdomain?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">If it is newly created and will send at scale: yes. Reputation attaches to the sending identity, including subdomains.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Can warm-up tools help?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Engagement-based warm-up (automatic replies to simulated mail) has limited, debated value. Real engagement from real recipients is the durable path.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">What volume is 'safe' immediately?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Small: tens to low hundreds per day from a new identity. Volume is earned, not configured.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">Does DMARC need to be at reject before warm-up?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">No: p=none with reporting is correct during warm-up; enforcement comes after the identity stabilizes.</p></details><details class="group rounded-xl border border-line bg-panel/60 px-5 py-4 open:border-accent/40"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-ink [&::-webkit-details-marker]:hidden">My warm-up was fine but mail went to spam in week 3. Why?<span class="text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45">+</span></summary><p class="mt-3 text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-dim">Volume outgrew engagement, or a content/link change tripped filters. Cut volume in half, raise engagement, then resume.</p></details></div>
      <h2 class="font-display mt-10 text-xl font-semibold text-ink">Related</h2>
      <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-2"><li><a href="/dedicated-vs-shared-ip/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Dedicated vs shared IP →</a></li><li><a href="/why-emails-go-to-spam/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Why emails go to spam →</a></li><li><a href="/email-deliverability/" class="text-accent hover:text-accent-soft">Email deliverability hub →</a></li></ul>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
